  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-64489\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>Recall that:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>A unit circle has a radius of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"2\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> and is centered at the origin in the coordinate plane.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>An angle in the standard position has its initial side on the positive <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"3\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>-axis and a vertex that lies on the origin. </p>\n</li>\n<li><p>A positive angle has a rotation that is measured counter-clockwise.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Therefore, the correct diagram is as follows:</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-q-64489-e-0\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-64489-e-0\"></div></div>",
